OL,3,ABurnham brands ban on football fans
OL,4,Adrinking alcohol in stands as
OL,5,A'discrimination'
OL,6,
OL,7,FAndy Burnham has branded a ban on fans
OL,8,Fbeing allowed to drink alcohol in the
OL,9,Fstands during men's football matches as
OL,10,F"discrimination".
OL,12,FThe prime minister told reporters that
OL,13,F"I don't think it's fair for football
OL,14,Ffans to be singled out", as he
OL,15,Fsuggested a change could be trialled.
OL,17,FLaws are in place which prevent
OL,18,Fdrinking in view of the pitch at
OL,19,Fstadiums for clubs in the top five
OL,20,Ftiers of men's football in England.
OL,21,FOther sports do not face such a
OL,22,Frestriction.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
